                    insight_sustainable:    `Sustainable scaling: you reached ARR ≥€2.4M with the product and customer base healthy and runway intact. You scaled the product before the distribution — growth that compounds instead of leaking.`,
                    insight_runout:         `You ran out of runway. Scaling distribution ahead of the product on a 12-month aggressive burn, with no guaranteed next round, is the irreversible risk the case warned about. Cash is the one constraint you can't recover from.`,
                    insight_sand:           `Growth on sand: ARR rose but product and customer health stayed weak. You filled a leaky bucket faster — the headline ARR is fragile and the churn will claw it back.`,
                    insight_notready:       `You never reached scale-readiness. Product and customer health stayed below the thresholds that make expansion safe — you optimised for speed over the base that growth has to stand on.`,
                    insight_churn:          `Customer health stayed low: high churn and concentration mean every new customer you add leaks back out. Sales spend without fixing churn is a faster leak, not faster growth.`,
                    insight_product:        `Product health stayed weak — the platform never earned the right to scale. New markets and 3x load on a 99.2%-uptime monolith multiply incidents and churn.`,
                    insight_aggressive:     `You took the aggressive capture plan and the 12-month runway came due. The lesson the facilitator pressed: scaling distribution before the product multiplies churn, not revenue.`,
                    insight_milestones:     `This is milestone-based growth done right: you served the fund's 3–5x horizon and the founder's 10-year survival at once, with written triggers that accelerate and brake on real metrics.`,

                    hint_runout:            `Runway has collapsed to the 12-month floor or below. The aggressive burn with no guaranteed round is the irreversible risk — cut burn, protect cash, don't bet the company on a future raise.`,
                    hint_aggressive:        `You chose aggressive capture; churn is now eating the ARR. Refund the product and fix customer health, or the 12-month runway runs out before the growth pays off.`,
                    hint_churn:             `Customer health is dangerously low — you're scaling a leaky bucket. Shield the anchor accounts and lower churn before spending more on new logos.`,
                    hint_product:           `Product health is weak — the platform can't hold the load you're adding. Fund the re-platform before opening any new market.`,
                    hint_behind:            `You're behind on scale-readiness with little time left. Concentrate on product stability and customer concentration — the base expansion has to stand on.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — product, customer and runway all healthy. Now lock in written milestone triggers so growth accelerates and brakes on real numbers.`,

